# Purpose
Support PWA features (installable, push notifications) and web deployment best practices. App runs in browser on web; mobile-optimized via responsive design.

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO serve over HTTPS in production (required for PWA, service workers, push).
DO include a web app manifest (manifest.json) with name, short_name, icons, start_url, display.
DO register a service worker for offline/caching and push notifications (e.g., Firebase Cloud Messaging).
DO use relative or environment-based URLs for API base; never hardcode production URLs.
DO ensure icons exist for common sizes (192×192, 512×512) for PWA install prompt.

### DON'T
MUST NOT assume native app capabilities; use web APIs (Web Push, Notifications) for push.
MUST NOT block initial render for non-critical PWA setup; lazy-load service worker registration.
MUST NOT cache API responses indefinitely without invalidation strategy.

## PWA Checklist
[ ] manifest.json present with required fields.
[ ] Service worker registered (e.g., Workbox, custom).
[ ] HTTPS in production.
[ ] Icons for 192px and 512px.
